Decode SGR mouse events when the screen library ate the prefix.

Clicking in the panels did nothing and left droppings like "5;16M" on the
screen: the tail of an SGR 1006 mouse report, "\e[<0;5;16M", decoded by the
legacy parser and partly echoed as text.

mc always turns SGR 1006 reporting on (lib/tty/mouse.c), so every event
arrives in SGR form, but it can reach xmouse_get_event() by two routes. If
mc's own key tree matches "\e[<" the event is correctly marked extended. If
the terminfo "kmous" capability happens to be "\e[<" as well, ncurses matches
it first, swallows the prefix and hands back KEY_MOUSE - and the test that
recognises that case requires xmouse_seq to be NULL, which it never is,
because tty_init_xterm_support() has just rewritten it from "\e[<" to "\e[M"
a few lines earlier. So the event is decoded as legacy X10.

Which route is taken depends entirely on the terminfo entry. ncurses 5.x
described xterm with kmous=\E[M, while ncurses 6.x resolves xterm-256color
through the xterm+sm+1006 building block, where kmous=\E[<. Hence a build
that carries its own recent terminfo loses the mouse, and the same mc built
against an older one does not.

Record whether kmous was the SGR sequence and use that to mark the event
extended, leaving the existing NULL case alone.

--- a/lib/tty/mouse.h
+++ b/lib/tty/mouse.h
@@ -103,6 +103,11 @@
 /* String indicating that an SGR extended mouse event has occurred, namely "\E[<" */
 extern const char *xmouse_extended_seq;
 
+/* TRUE when the terminfo "kmous" capability was the SGR sequence "\E[<" rather
+   than the legacy "\E[M", which means the screen library consumes the prefix
+   itself and the event that reaches us is in SGR form. */
+extern gboolean xmouse_kmous_is_sgr;
+
 /*** declarations of public functions ************************************************************/
 
 /* General (i.e. both for xterm and gpm) mouse support definitions */
--- a/lib/tty/mouse.c
+++ b/lib/tty/mouse.c
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@
 int mouse_fd = -1;              /* for when gpm_fd changes to < 0 and the old one must be cleared from select_set */
 const char *xmouse_seq;
 const char *xmouse_extended_seq;
+gboolean xmouse_kmous_is_sgr = FALSE;
 
 /*** file scope macro definitions ****************************************************************/
 
--- a/lib/tty/tty.c
+++ b/lib/tty/tty.c
@@ -408,7 +408,10 @@
     if (xmouse_seq != NULL)
     {
         if (strcmp (xmouse_seq, ESC_STR "[<") == 0)
+        {
             xmouse_seq = ESC_STR "[M";
+            xmouse_kmous_is_sgr = TRUE;
+        }
 
         xmouse_extended_seq = ESC_STR "[<";
     }
--- a/lib/tty/key.c
+++ b/lib/tty/key.c
@@ -2107,8 +2107,8 @@
         gboolean extended = c == MCKEY_EXTENDED_MOUSE;
 
 #ifdef KEY_MOUSE
-        extended = extended || (c == KEY_MOUSE && xmouse_seq == NULL
-                                && xmouse_extended_seq != NULL);
+        extended = extended || (c == KEY_MOUSE && xmouse_extended_seq != NULL
+                                && (xmouse_seq == NULL || xmouse_kmous_is_sgr));
 #endif /* KEY_MOUSE */
 
         xmouse_get_event (event, extended);
